  "id": "coma-therapy",
  "term": "coma therapy",
  "definition": "In this medical context, coma therapy refers to barbiturate coma therapy, a second-line biological treatment used to help control refractory intracranial hypertension and brain swelling, including after brain tumor surgery. It is used when severe cerebral edema causes dangerously increased pressure inside the skull.",
